WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
From 10 to noon, a storm surge may flood low metro vancouver shores. This is vancouver daily, episode 52. I'm Mira, the Nerranetwork's AI host. I don't live in vancouver. After that, care home flew outbreaks, a homicide investigation in wali, and a hotel fight on sea more street, then getting around. After this week's storms pushed water levels up, the new warning is as surge as the rain eases. Environment Canada says it could reach low, expose shores and metro vancouver.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:39.080
South East Vancouver Island and the southern Gulf Islands with water above the predicted tide from high winds and what the agency calls enhanced wave activity.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:43.640
CBC carries the same Friday warning for Metro Vancouver in greater Victoria.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:50.000
Most rainfall warnings lifted Thursday, though two yellow warnings remain for Western and inland Vancouver Island.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.540
heaviest near Zabalos and Tahassas into late this afternoon.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.300
Parts of the southwest have already taken more than 300 millimeters.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:00.060
People north of Squamish are sheltering in place.

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:02.740
Pemberton is still under an evacuation alert,

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.380
with parts of the village under an evacuation order.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:09.180
And orders are also in place for the Lilwatt First Nation and for Zabalos.

00:01:10.563 --> 00:01:13.903
Influenza is running hotter in BC than almost anywhere in Canada,

00:01:14.303 --> 00:01:16.883
and it is already inside lower mainland care homes.

00:01:17.363 --> 00:01:19.743
Federal data put the province in the high category,

00:01:19.743 --> 00:01:26.183
with between 17.8 and 27.4% of lab tests positive and only Nunavut higher.

00:01:26.783 --> 00:01:30.783
Dr. Brian Conway, medical director of the Vancouver Infectious Disease Center,

00:01:31.083 --> 00:01:36.143
told Post Media the spread looks tied to a mutated H1N1 strain of influenza A

00:01:36.143 --> 00:01:41.403
that passes a little more easily and that people 65 and older are still most of the cases.

00:01:41.923 --> 00:01:45.523
Fraser Health lists 12 active outbreaks at long-term care homes,

00:01:45.843 --> 00:01:48.523
declared between October 23 and November 10.

00:01:48.523 --> 00:01:53.523
Vancouver Coastal Health List 5, foreign care homes, and one at a hospital in

00:01:53.523 --> 00:01:58.883
Seshalt. A BC Center for Disease Control report published November 4, found 82

00:01:58.883 --> 00:02:06.123
of 363 sentinel samples from August 30 to October 24 positive, a 23% rate, and

00:02:06.123 --> 00:02:10.663
the center called the week of October 25 to the 31st moderate, against low in

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:16.683
that week last year. Since August 30, federal figures show 1,699 influenza

00:02:16.683 --> 00:02:22.863
influenza-associated hospitalizations, 77 intensive care admissions, and 31 deaths, with hospital

00:02:22.863 --> 00:02:28.903
numbers covering 83% of Canadians, and intensive care and death numbers covering 22%.

00:02:28.903 --> 00:02:33.123
Conway said the BC shot should still give meaningful protection against severe illness

00:02:33.123 --> 00:02:36.443
from this strain, and that peak protection takes about two weeks.

00:02:36.943 --> 00:02:40.983
Pharmacy appointments can be booked at 1-8-338-2323.

00:02:42.056 --> 00:02:46.596
Surrey Police called in the Integrated Homicide Investigation Team after a man was shot

00:02:46.596 --> 00:02:53.056
and killed Thursday morning at a home in the 10,600 block of 132nd Street. Attempts to revive him

00:02:53.056 --> 00:02:58.676
failed. Sergeant Ali Gailas said officers in BC emergency health services reached the Wally House

00:02:58.676 --> 00:03:03.696
at about 716 for a man with an apparent gunshot wound, and that he was pronounced dead there.

00:03:04.216 --> 00:03:08.436
The homicide team has the file and wants anyone with information or video to call its

00:03:08.436 --> 00:03:14.700
information line. Surrey's website now lists senior staff and acting roles after Mayor Doug McCallum's

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.960
election, and the city will not confirm the changes or say why.

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:23.380
Benji Lee is listed as Acting City Solicitor, a job Philip Hoon held before the election.

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:28.860
Fire Chief Jason Kierney is also listed as Acting General Manager of Public Safety, a

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:30.140
job Brian Edwards held.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:35.760
Former Mayor Brenda Locke appointed Edwards to that post in 2025 after he had been in charge

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.040
of the Surrey RCMP.

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:42.380
At Council this week, Hoon, Edwards and City Manager Rob Costanzo were not there.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:47.220
Counselor Harry Baines, the only member left from Locke's Council, said neither the

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:51.540
mayor nor the other counselors had spoken to him about it, and he asked how much severance

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:52.140
is being paid.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:57.620
He noted Locke's team waited nine months after October 2022 to change the city manager.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:03.320
Media relations told Post Media the city cannot comment on personnel matters because of privacy.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:09.180
McCallum and Deputy Mayor Counselor Mandip Nagra did not answer questions, and unsigned

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:14.740
email to counselors, sent in the name of engineering, planning, corporate services and legal staff,

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:19.620
called the first week absolutely disgraceful, and the handling of jobs borderline criminal.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:24.260
Messages to Edwards and Hoon bounced, and an auto reply said the mayor's assistant,

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:32.520
Harp Dylan, is no longer available. The 2025 salary filing lists Hoon at a base of $228,227,

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:42.440
dollars, plus 52,475 in benefits. Edwards at 99,849, plus 7,844 for a partial year that

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:52.280
started at the end of August 2025. Castanzo at a base of 426,821, plus 122,277 in benefits.

00:04:52.780 --> 00:05:02.182
And Dillon at a 2025 base of 102,655, plus 14,540. An unfinished Surrey City Center Tower

00:05:02.182 --> 00:05:04.842
is on the market for $30 million by court order.

00:05:05.242 --> 00:05:09.502
The center project at $13,862.101 avenue

00:05:09.502 --> 00:05:11.782
reached six stories of a plan 24.

00:05:12.402 --> 00:05:15.422
Goodman Commercial is selling it for receiver Alvarez and Marseille.

00:05:15.902 --> 00:05:19.862
The 1.2 acre site, about a 13-minute walk from King George Station

00:05:19.862 --> 00:05:24.862
was approved for 167 strata homes and 194 parking stalls.

00:05:25.322 --> 00:05:29.282
Goodman says more than $23 million has already gone into hard construction

00:05:29.282 --> 00:05:34.442
and the ask works out to about $206 per square foot of approved buildable area.

00:05:34.942 --> 00:05:39.422
The July 2025 assessment role put the value at $26.71 million.

00:05:39.982 --> 00:05:44.862
The Supreme Court of British Columbia appointed the receiver in March 2026 over Central

00:05:44.862 --> 00:05:47.962
Limited Partnership and other entities linked to the Everest Group.

00:05:48.382 --> 00:05:54.882
A December 2025 petition from Domain Mortgage Corporation for capstone lenders said $27.8

00:05:54.882 --> 00:06:01.502
million was advanced in March 2022 at 14% a year, and that about 44.2 million was owing,

00:06:01.742 --> 00:06:04.162
with about 15.2 million in builder's means.

00:06:04.882 --> 00:06:07.182
Work had been stopped since late summer 2024.

00:06:07.722 --> 00:06:12.902
By the receivership date, the receiver later reported about 45.7 million on the capstone

00:06:12.902 --> 00:06:19.202
financing, 8.9 million to Desjardins, and 11.5 million to contractor Metrocan, which

00:06:19.202 --> 00:06:22.602
walked away in December 2025 because it had not been paid.

00:06:23.502 --> 00:06:26.522
152 of the 167 homes had been pre-sold.

00:06:27.082 --> 00:06:31.322
Those deals are cancelled, and the site is being offered for a fresh condo sales program

00:06:31.322 --> 00:06:32.622
or for market rental.

00:06:33.725 --> 00:06:40.325
Vancouver City staff want the new council to refuse a 15-story hotel at 852-872 Seymour

00:06:40.325 --> 00:06:44.145
Street, mid-blocked between Robson and Smith across from the Orphium.

00:06:44.665 --> 00:06:47.365
The referral report is on the November 17th agenda.

00:06:47.365 --> 00:06:52.485
Staff, in a rare move, won a later public hearing and a recommendation to reject the Benning

00:06:52.485 --> 00:06:55.225
Group Plan, designed by Arno Mattis' Architecture.

00:06:55.665 --> 00:07:00.785
It would keep the two-story front of the 1926 Great War Veterans Association Hall, hold

00:07:00.785 --> 00:07:05.645
151 guest rooms, and put a 2,500-square-foot restaurant and bar on the street.

00:07:06.105 --> 00:07:14.045
The building would be 163 feet and about 82,500-square feet, 11 times a lot of roughly 7,500-square

00:07:14.045 --> 00:07:19.225
feet, with about 18 stalls on two underground levels, reached by car elevators off the lane.

00:07:19.725 --> 00:07:24.765
The last council protected that facade in 2023, and staff say this preservation is enough.

00:07:25.305 --> 00:07:30.225
The hall later held LGBTQ nightclubs, including playpin central and Hollywood north.

00:07:30.765 --> 00:07:35.685
When the Marriott next door was approved in 2023, this lot was expected to carry about seven

00:07:35.685 --> 00:07:36.185
stories.

00:07:36.605 --> 00:07:43.125
That 30-story 390-room Moxie and Elements Tower is under construction at 848 Seymour, and

00:07:43.125 --> 00:07:44.965
and is expected to open in 2028.

00:07:45.445 --> 00:07:47.745
Seven of its rooms would look only into a light well

00:07:47.745 --> 00:07:49.305
on the new hotel's north side.

00:07:49.845 --> 00:07:51.905
Staff say those rooms would not get enough daylight,

00:07:52.405 --> 00:07:53.825
sunlight, or a real view out.

00:07:54.185 --> 00:07:56.565
And the Marriott developer has raised serious concerns.

00:07:57.145 --> 00:07:59.485
South of the lot, the frontage is 62 feet

00:07:59.485 --> 00:08:00.865
and the depth about 120.

00:08:01.525 --> 00:08:03.985
The design leaves as little as a 36-foot gap

00:08:03.985 --> 00:08:09.125
to the 29th story Vita Tower at 565 Smith, built in 2009.

00:08:09.645 --> 00:08:12.045
Short of the usual 60-foot separation from homes

00:08:12.045 --> 00:08:14.585
that is meant to keep privacy, daylight, and sky.

00:08:15.265 --> 00:08:17.665
Staff say meeting that gap here means a shorter building.

00:08:18.145 --> 00:08:21.305
The drawings use privacy glass and a vine wall on the south face.

00:08:21.945 --> 00:08:26.325
Staff grant that more hotel rooms help, and still say this shape would clash with the hotel

00:08:26.325 --> 00:08:27.425
in the homes beside it.

00:08:27.885 --> 00:08:32.125
Council can approve anyway, and the report includes draft zoning and conditions for that.

00:08:32.585 --> 00:08:37.025
A hearing is not required by law, but staff want one because of public comment and the two

00:08:37.025 --> 00:08:37.305
neighbors.

00:08:37.305 --> 00:08:43.125
Their September 2026 count says the city is on pace for 10,000 net new rooms, seven

00:08:43.125 --> 00:08:50.365
rezoning's under review with 1,480 rooms, 13 approved rezoning's with 3,380, four

00:08:50.365 --> 00:08:56.045
projects with 1,060 still in permits, six under construction with 1,010, and eight

00:08:56.045 --> 00:09:02.185
just finished with 540, about 7,500 rooms and 38 projects. Destination Vancouver

00:09:02.185 --> 00:09:07.285
estimates 20,000 net new rooms are needed across Metro Vancouver, 10,000 of them in

00:09:07.285 --> 00:09:13.405
the city. The region has about 25,000 hotel rooms now, 13,000 in Vancouver, fewer than

00:09:13.405 --> 00:09:18.025
in the early 2000s. Staff say high-building costs make it uncertain how many of those

00:09:18.025 --> 00:09:23.045
approvals will actually get built. Also on the board, RCMP are investigating a fatal

00:09:23.045 --> 00:09:27.545
